---
/**
 * A coach's public profile.
 *
 * ONE STATIC PAGE SERVING EVERY HANDLE. `/c/andreas_p` is rewritten onto this
 * route by netlify.toml — a 200, not a redirect, so the address the coach shared
 * stays in the bar. The island reads `location.pathname` to find out who it is
 * showing. This is exactly how `/s/<id>` serves the shared viewer, and the
 * reasoning for the rewrite target being the ROUTE rather than the built HTML
 * file is written out next to that rule.
 *
 * `noindex` FOR NOW, and the reason is the same one on /studio/watch/: there is
 * no page here to index, only a shell that fills itself in on the client, and
 * every handle would otherwise look to a crawler like a duplicate of every
 * other one. Phase 2 of docs/SOCIAL.md makes this route server-rendered, and
 * that is the commit where the noindex comes off and the OG card goes on.
 *
 * NOT `bare`. The shared viewer hides the site nav because a coach presenting
 * off it in front of a room does not want it; a profile is the opposite — it is
 * somebody's shop window, and the nav is the way a visitor who liked what they
 * saw finds out what this place is.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import PublicProfile from '../../studio/account/PublicProfile'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Profile"
  description="A coach on Total Football."
  path="/c/"
  noindex
>
  {/* A `div`, not a `<main>`. BaseLayout already provides `<main id="main">`
      around the slot, and a nested one is invalid HTML — the studio pages that
      do it predate this and are left alone rather than quietly rewritten. */}
  <div class="min-h-[70vh] bg-paper-deep">
    <PublicProfile client:only="react" />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
